course: dictionary
lesson: 15939
title: Unselfish
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Unselfish» describes someone who thinks about other people's needs and is happy to share or help. It means you are not only thinking of yourself. Look for clues in the sentence: words like gave, shared, or helped often show that someone is being unselfish.
explain: «Maya gave her last biscuit to her little brother, even though she was still hungry.» Giving away your last biscuit is a kind thing to do, and it puts someone else first. So Maya is unselfish.
explain: Stories often show unselfish characters. In The Wind in the Willows, Rat takes Mole home, even though Rat wants to get back himself. Ask yourself: what would a selfish person do here? Then check your answer by swapping in unselfish and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Unselfish» means thinking about other people's needs and being happy to share or help.
fact: The opposite of unselfish is selfish, which means thinking only of yourself.
fact: Unselfish acts, like sharing your lunch or letting a younger child go first, are often praised in stories and in lessons about values.
fact: In team games, an unselfish player passes the ball to a teammate who is in a better position.
exercise: «Sam let his little sister go first on the slide.» Which word describes Sam? | Lazy | Bored | Noisy | *Unselfish
exercise: «Mia passed the ball to a teammate who was free, instead of shooting herself.» What kind of player is she? | Greedy | *Unselfish | Careless | Angry
exercise: What does unselfish mean? | Very loud | Very tired | Thinking only of yourself | *Thinking about other people's needs and happy to share or help
test: «Priya gave up her seat on the bus for an old man.» Priya is being... | *Unselfish | Silly | Bored | Rude
test: Why is Rat unselfish when he takes Mole home? | He is bored of the river | He is angry with Mole | *He takes Mole home even though he wants to get back himself | He wants to rest at Mole's house
exam: «Tom gave his best pencil to a friend who had forgotten his, even though he needed it.» Which word describes Tom? | *Unselfish | Careful | Selfish | Lonely
